 Stacked on #8002 → #8000 → #7999 → #7998 → main; all hand-offs. Block 05 = the monotone-order class: one formation law for every linear extension of the product order (every rule); rows and columns path chains; the 2×2 corner law with corner independence; no right/down turning staircase is first-order Markov in its site values (proved for every nonconstant positive orbit triple under the declared product-rule monotone law); opposite corner classes give the same finite-rectangle law, with two distinct laws only at the executed 2×3 triples; the snake keeps rows and can lose column chains (column 0 survives on 3×3; on the executed 4×3 no column is a chain). Lens before the primary caught the supervisor's own wrong snake control. Historical checker: FIX FIRST on one forbidden mechanism sentence (false; deleted), nothing refuted in the theorems. Lock released.
 
 Current source review found five further P2 groups, corrected in the canonical note and runner with their disposition in REVIEW_HISTORY.md. Same-session confirmation is pending; this appendix records an open review handoff.
+
+## 2026-09-17 block 33 opened for review (supervisor; continuing "pick up the next in the queue")
+Independent PR against `main` (`9a3ffc8d91`); parent on `main`: block 01. Block 33 = the `c = 1` obligation attacked as an existence proof by induction on levels through the rooted value `v(z)`. Proved: the extension lemma (`v(z) ≤ 1 + v(u)`; amplified `−1 + v(u)`) and the seed lemma (`v(z) ≤ v(p) − 1` by a fork placed below the seed's level; two seeds `−2`); the induction closes at every site except a processed one all of whose 1-predecessors are tight (`v = 0`), so **the unit budget `E ≤ 3(|S| − 1) + |A|` at every realization is equivalent to the tight-sibling lemma** (open). Executed: the rooted inequality at all `788` sites of `140` tiny realizations (exact) and on `~10⁴` realizations of the climbs; the tight-sibling case never observed; the extremal roots have all predecessors at `−1`. Second lever: optimal trees never have two processed children at a node; the restricted count has exact certificates at `p ≥ 2921` (`c = 2`, a third below block 30) and `p ≥ 405` (`c = 1`), **not claimed** — the restriction is admissible on every executed realization at `c = 1` but costs one unit on `W3` at `c = 2`, so an exchange proof is excluded and an existence proof is needed. Records: `RESULTS_block33.md`, `CHECKER_block33_findings.md`, `CLAIM_STATUS_CERTIFICATE_block33.md`, `GOAL_block33.md`; specs with outputs. Campaign PRs open: blocks 12–32 (#8146–#8158, #8168, #8170–#8176), none merged, none commented. Queue after block 33: (1) the tight-sibling lemma (a local statement about the marks around a site whose supports are all saturated; the exact programs are the oracle); (2) an existence proof that a tree with the budget and at most one processed child per node exists (worth `4165 → 2921` at the proved budget); (3) a count that is not a union bound over sub-structures; (4) the sphere law's strong-coupling proof; spin-wave theory as a theorem; the torus memory time.
+
+## 2026-09-17 block 33 opened for review as PR #8177 (supervisor)
+PR #8177 (base `main`, independent). Records: `RESULTS_block33.md`, `CHECKER_block33_findings.md`, `CLAIM_STATUS_CERTIFICATE_block33.md`, `GOAL_block33.md`; specs with outputs. Campaign PRs open: blocks 12–33 (#8146–#8158, #8168, #8170–#8177), none merged, none commented. The `c = 1` obligation is one local lemma; the restricted count is one existence statement; both have exact oracles in the runner and the specs.
