@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# RESULTS — block 33: the rooted inequality reduces the unit budget to the tight-sibling lemma; the one-processed-child count with exact certificates at `p ≥ 2921` (c = 2) and `p ≥ 405` (c = 1), neither claimed (2026-09-17)
+
+**Deliverables (branch `physics-loop/admissibility-induced-law-block33-rooted-inequality-tight-sibling-lemma-one-processed-child-count-20260917`, independent PR against `main` at `9a3ffc8d91`; parent on `main`: block 01):** the note `docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_SIX_AXIS_FORMATION_THRESHOLD_THE_ROOTED_INEQUALITY_REDUCES_THE_UNIT_BUDGET_TO_THE_TIGHT_SIBLING_LEMMA_AND_THE_ONE_PROCESSED_CHILD_COUNT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-17.md`; the runner `scripts/admissibility_rule_six_axis_formation_threshold_rooted_inequality_reduces_the_unit_budget_to_the_tight_sibling_lemma_and_the_one_processed_child_count_2026_09_17.py` (18 checks, 7 mutations, exact, two seconds; exact rooted brute force on tiny realizations; the single-seed program with a level cap; the restricted recursion and its certificates); the pinned cache; the controls (`specs/supervisor_control_block33_{mintree,rooted,tight,lemmas,tightpairs,violate,shape,shape2,restricted_count,kind_certs,diag,certify33}.py`) and the refuting pass (`..._refuter.py`) with outputs; `GOAL_block33.md`; `CHECKER_block33_findings.md`; this record; `CLAIM_STATUS_CERTIFICATE_block33.md`; appends to the shared records.
+
+**Result.**
+- T1 (proved): extension lemma `v(z) ≤ 1 + v(u)` (amplified: `−1 + v(u)`); seed lemma `v(z) ≤ v(p) − 1` for a processed site with a seed 1-predecessor `s` and another 1-predecessor `w` with 1-predecessor `p` (the fork `s—w` placed above a tree rooted at `p`, which lies below the seed's level); two seed predecessors `−2`. Inductive step: the rooted inequality (`v ≤ 0` processed, `≤ −1` amplified) propagates to every site except a processed one whose 1-predecessors are all tight (`v = 0`). Hence the unit budget at every realization (block 32's `c* = 1`; `p ≥ 453`) **is equivalent to the tight-sibling lemma**: such a site has a rooted tree of cost `≤ 0`. Open.
+- Executed: on `140` tiny realizations (exact rooted brute force) the lemmas' instances hold (`357` pairs, `121` amplified, `15 + 78` seed cases), the inequality holds at all `788` sites, the tight-sibling case never arises; on the extremal realizations the tight roots have all three 1-predecessors at `−1` (T2); seeded and random climbs (about `10⁴` realizations) find no violation and no two tight siblings (largest `min(v(w₁), v(w₂))` from random starts `−2`; `−1` on `Z_A`).
+- T3 (exact): optimal trees never have two processed children at a node; the restricted recursion (`(1 + xU)^n → (1 + x_A U)^n + n x_P U (1 + x_A U)^{n−1}`) has exact super-solutions at `(2921,1,2)`, `(1464,1,1)`, `(5841,2,4)`, `(4380,1,3)` with `c = 2` and `(405,1,2)`, `(208,1,1)`, `(810,2,4)`, `(605,1,3)` with `c = 1`; the same code with the full factor is block 25's recursion and passes block 30's certificate; the kind-typed eight-variable count reproduces `4165/2085` and `453/232` and reduces to three variables.
+- T4 (executed): the restriction is admissible on `60` tiny realizations (brute force) and on `125` realizations at `c = 1` (integer program), but at `c = 2` block 31's `W3` has a restricted minimum `−61` against `−62`: not cost-free, so no exchange proof; neither region claimed.
+
+**What this changes.** The `c = 1` obligation is now a single local lemma with an oracle; the restricted count is a second, independent lever (a third off block 30's coupling at the proved budget) waiting on an existence statement. Blocks 30–32 stand.
+
+**Seats.** Supervisor-run: lens (construction → existence by induction) → controls (rooted values; hard cases; candidate lemmas; climbs; shape; the kind-typed count, first divergent by a missing own-arrow term, then by the wrong start point, then exact; eight-variable certificates failed on scaling, three-variable certificates found) → contract → primary (T1–T4, runner) → refuting pass (integer program vs exact program; the seed lemma's trees verified independently; eight- and three-variable fixed points against the certificate; an adversarial climb on the extension lemma) → fold (seeds' rooted value `≤ 0`, not `= 0`: sibling seeds joined by forks) → census 7/7 in-family → gates → PR.
+
+**Addendum (2026-09-17, after PR opening).** Block 30's construction itself produces the two-processed-children pattern rarely (`0–3` nodes per `2100` trees; at seeds, amplified and processed targets; never three processed children) and a modified excuse rule does not remove it (the remaining cases are forced: both poles have a single valid excuse). "At most two processed children per node" is worth only `4165 → 4041` in the count, so the one-child restriction (`2921`) stands or falls with an existence proof. The rooted-value profile of `Z_A`/`Z_B` (`specs/supervisor_control_block33_vprofile.out.txt`) shows `v` as a staircase distance: `+1` per processed step, `−1` per amplified step, with `v(z) = 1 + min_u v(u)` at `34` of `45` processed sites of `Z_B` (merges or harvests help at the rest); a tight site is the top of a staircase exactly as tall as the harvest below it. Controls: `..._doublechild2.py`, `..._doublekind.py`, `..._vprofile.py` (with `..._core30.py`, block 30's construction restated) and outputs.
+
+**Addendum 2 (2026-09-17, later).** A structural search for the open case — moves that duplicate a band of marks translated by a sibling or predecessor offset, so that a break-even support is placed beside itself — run for twenty minutes in four boxes (`6×6×8`, `6×6×9`, `7×7×8`, `5×5×10`) from the extremal realizations: no processed site with all 1-predecessors tight, no rooted value above `0`, at most two tight sites in any configuration and never as siblings (`specs/supervisor_control_block33_structural.py`, `.out.txt`). The overlap measurement (`..._overlap.py`) shows why the tight roots are tight: the optimal supports of their predecessors overlap in harvest-rich sets (`E_O − A_O = −2` to `−4` on `Z_A`, `−3` on `Z_B`), so the union of two supports costs more than one of them; a violation would need two tight siblings whose supports overlap in the same way, which the search does not produce.
